Planar 3R SNS Controller (ROS2)
A ROS2 Jazzy package implementing kinematic control of a planar 3-link redundant robot arm using the Saturation in the Null Space (SNS) algorithm (Flacco, De Luca & Khatib, 2015), ported from the author's MSc dissertation MATLAB/Python implementation and validated in simulation and on a physical 7-DOF Franka Research 3 robot.

What this does
Defines the robot as a URDF (link lengths matching the dissertation's planar 3R model: 1.0 m / 0.8 m / 0.6 m)
Visualises the robot live in RViz2
Runs a custom ROS2 node (sns_controller) that:
Computes forward kinematics and the analytical Jacobian
Commands the end-effector along a circular trajectory
Applies an SNS-style pseudoinverse control law with joint velocity limits, publishing live sensor_msgs/JointState messages
Background
This project extends work from the author's MSc dissertation, "Null-Space Saturation with Dynamic Task Priorities for Redundant Robot Control" (Kingston University London, 2026), which implemented and experimentally validated the SNS and GSNS algorithms on a physical Franka Research 3 robot arm. See [dissertation summary / link] for details and physical hardware results.

